<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    The narrowest configuration that still answers "which app just opened?".

    Every line here is a promise made on the disclosure screen the parent consents
    to before this permission is ever requested, and Google Play reads this file
    when it reviews an AccessibilityService. A capability declared here and not used
    is a rejection waiting to happen; a capability used and not declared simply does
    not work. So the two are kept identical on purpose.

      * accessibilityEventTypes = typeWindowStateChanged only. Not typeViewClicked,
        not typeViewTextChanged, not typeWindowContentChanged - none of which we
        need and all of which would carry what the child is doing inside an app.

      * canRetrieveWindowContent = false. This is the line that makes "Lunio does
        not read the screen" true in code rather than only in the privacy policy
        (Art. 14). It also means the service cannot see text fields, so a password
        typed while it is running is not something we could read even by mistake.

      * no android:packageNames. The filter is the parent's list, evaluated in
        BlockPolicy, not a static list compiled into the app - the parent chooses
        which apps are blocked, and that choice changes after install.

      * notificationTimeout = 0. This attribute throttles delivery of same-type
        events; Article 11.2 allows two seconds from the game appearing to the block
        landing, and spending any of it on deliberate throttling would be a choice
        we could not defend at acceptance.
-->
<accessibility-service xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:description="@string/lunio_a11y_description"
    android:summary="@string/lunio_a11y_summary"
    android:accessibilityEventTypes="typeWindowStateChanged"
    android:accessibilityFeedbackType="feedbackGeneric"
    android:accessibilityFlags="flagDefault"
    android:canRetrieveWindowContent="false"
    android:notificationTimeout="0" />
